  "notes": "{温度|おんど} (temperature) + {計|けい} (meter, gauge). The general word for any device that measures temperature, whether a medical thermometer, a room thermometer, or an industrial temperature gauge.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {温度計|おんどけい}で{測|はか}る — measure with a thermometer\n- {温度計|おんどけい}の{目盛|めも}り — scale on a thermometer\n- {温度計|おんどけい}が{上|あ}がる — the thermometer rises\n- {温度計|おんどけい}が{下|さ}がる — the thermometer drops\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {体温計|たいおんけい} — clinical thermometer (specifically for body temperature)\n- {寒暖計|かんだんけい} — thermometer (older term, emphasizing hot and cold)\n- {湿度計|しつどけい} — hygrometer (humidity meter)\n- {気圧計|きあつけい} — barometer",
